<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi Cairo Bank nine-month net declines.</title>
<headline>Saudi Cairo Bank nine-month net declines.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Cairo Bank on Monday issued the following results for the nine months to September 30, 1996:</p>
<p>			   (million Saudi riyals unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit		    165.8	     vs  178.2</p>
<p> Operating income	    793.1	     vs  908.2</p>
<p> Operating expenses	  635.6	     vs  733.0</p>
<p> Net operating income	157.5	     vs  175.2</p>
<p> Other income		    8.3	     vs    2.9</p>
<p> Provision			30.0	     vs   30.0</p>
<p> Shareholders' funds	   1.75 billion  vs    1.66 billion</p>
<p> Total deposits		 11.59 billion  vs   14.81 billion</p>
<p> Assets			   16.38 billion  vs   20.50 billion</p>
<p>Full Name: Saudi Cairo Bank</p>
<p>Note - The bank is 55 percent owned by Saudi investors. The Saudi government's Public Investment Fund holds 25 percent and Egypt's Banque du Caire owns the remaining 20 percent.</p>
</text>
